COLLECTION HIERARCHY :

  -All the elements and classes present in java.util.package.
  - the entire java collection hierarchy around fore core interfaces and two specilized interfaces
     - Collection Interface
     - List Interface
     - Set Interface
     - Queue Interface
     - Map interface
     - Specialized Interface
        - SortedMap Interface
        - NavigableMap Interface

  - COLLECTION INTERFACE:
    - Collection Interface is root of interface of the java collection framework,
    it is the root of most of the collection  API.
    - Collection Interface Placed in top of the collection hierarchy in java.
    - The collection interface extends Iterable Interface in java.
    - The Iterable Interface contains only one method called Iterator(), function of the iterator method is to return
    Iterator object.
    - The List, Set and Queue Interface Extends The collection Interface.
    - Map Interface Not Extends to collection Interface. because Map store data in key value pair. It is differant in other collection type.

  - LIST INTERFACE :
    - List Interface Stores element are arranged sequentially order.
    - list interface stores duplicate elements.
    - In the list Interface you insert, access,insert and remove element from ant index.
    - The order of put think in is order you get them out.
    - There are three main subclass implement list Interface.
       - ArrayList 1.2v C
       - LinkedList 1.2v C
       - Vector  1.0 v LC
       - ant it is subclass Stack 1.0 v LC

  - SET INTERFACE:
     - The Set of Interface represent collection of elements contains unique elements.
     - Set Not Store Duplicate elements.
     - A Set Does not maintain order of Storing element.
